course: dictionary
lesson: 5459
title: Languid: slow and lazy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a whole picture. Languid describes something moving slowly and lazily, with little energy. Read the words around it to check: «The Caterpillar speaks in a languid, sleepy voice.» A sleepy voice is slow and soft, so languid fits. Try your meaning in the sentence: "a slow, lazy voice" still makes sense.
explain: Languid can describe a person, a day or a feeling. «a languid summer afternoon» is warm, calm and slow, with nothing rushing. A languid wave of the hand shows someone cannot be bothered to move much. Often the word feels pleasant, like lying in the sun, but it can also mean weak and tired, as when you are ill.
explain: The opposite of languid is energetic, brisk or lively. If someone is bouncing around with energy, they are not languid. Look for the clues: slow movement, quiet voice, warm still air.
fact: Languid means moving slowly and lazily, without much energy.
fact: Languid can also mean weak and tired, maybe from heat or illness.
fact: Languid can describe weather or days: «a languid summer afternoon» is slow, warm and calm.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the summer river and lazy afternoons have a languid feel.
fact: Opposites of languid include energetic, brisk and lively.
exercise: «The Caterpillar speaks in a languid, sleepy voice.» What does languid mean here? | Fast and excited | Loud and angry | Sharp and cold | *Slow and lazy
exercise: Which word is the opposite of languid? | Sleepy | Warm | *Energetic | Lazy
exercise: «A languid wave of the hand» shows what? | *Someone cannot be bothered | Someone is cold and wet | Someone is in a hurry to leave | Someone is very excited
test: «The children sat by the river on a languid afternoon, watching the water drift past.» What does languid mean? | Wet and cold | Loud and busy | *Slow, warm and calm | Sharp and bright
test: «Ella felt languid after a week of fever.» What does languid mean here? | *Weak and tired, without energy | Very loud | Quick and clever | Happy and full of games
exam: Mia says, "Languid is just another word for fast." Is she right? | *No, languid means slow and lazy, so fast is the opposite | Yes, they mean the same | Yes, but only in stories | Only on hot days
